ed that learning would spoil a slave, make him unmanageable, of no value to his master, and forever unfit him to be a slave, making him discontented and unhappy", "unit": null, "status": "extra"}, {"text": "Douglass resolved to learn anyway, since the opposition inspired his determination", "unit": null, "status": "extra"}, {"text": "His successful method was making friends of little white boys in the street, converting them into teachers, trading bread for lessons, until he finally succeeded in learning to read", "unit": "R3", "status": "duplicate"}], "reason": "All required claims are covered; extra details do not affect correctness."}
